      "placement": "before",
      "source": {
        "column": 3,
        "length": 79,
        "line": 65,
      },
      "text": "%% spec says "directly below", so the rows touch unless I add offset-y by hand.",
      "type": "comment",
    },
    {
      "attachTo": 28,
      "placement": "before",
      "source": {
        "column": 45,
        "length": 434,
        "line": 59,
      },
      "text": "

  %% GAP 3: second row. Auto top puts each figure below the previous sibling that shares
  %% its columns. These two share columns with different figures above, so their tops only
  %% line up because both figures above have the same fixed height. With ratio-based
  %% heights the row would be ragged. There is also no defined gap between rows: the
  %% spec says "directly below", so the rows touch unless I add offset-y by hand.
",
